From f020c79ceb204e91043da7627fcf280033bf2f50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Apr 2026 15:50:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] serial: stm32: spin_lock around
 stm32_usart_rx_dma_start_or_resume()

To protect the DMA RX resource, we add a spin lock around the
stm32_usart_rx_dma_start_or_resume() because it can run concurrently
with the stm32_usart_receive_chars() function.

Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ib4317afe3f9d04e8adfccf2657de9d6c6148f705
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/570586
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
@@ -2456,8 +2456,10 @@ static int __maybe_unused stm32_usart_se
 			stm32_usart_set_bits(port, ofs->cr3, USART_CR3_DMAT);
 
 		if (stm32_port->rx_ch) {
+			spin_lock_irqsave(&port->lock, flags);
 			stm32_usart_set_bits(port, ofs->cr3, USART_CR3_DMAR);
 			ret = stm32_usart_rx_dma_start_or_resume(port);
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&port->lock, flags);
 			if (ret)
 				return ret;
 		}
